    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 tests green).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `registrationDate` feature for owner creation. When a registration date is supplied on `POST /api/owners` it is kept; when omitted it defaults to the server's current date, and it is returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format.\n\nChanges, each placed at the layer it belongs to:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `registrationDate` (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema, mirroring the existing `birthDate` field. Because it lives on `OwnerFields`, the generated `OwnerFieldsDto` accepts it on input and `OwnerDto` returns it, and Jackson serializes the resulting `LocalDate` as `YYYY-MM-DD` (same as `birthDate`).\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `LocalDate registrationDate` column with its getter/setter, plus a `@PrePersist` hook that defaults it to `LocalDate.now()` only when null. `@PrePersist` fires solely on insert, so a supplied date is preserved and updates never overwrite it \u2014 and it works for any create path without duplicating logic in the controller.\n\n3. **`schema.sql`** (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table, keeping all four dialects consistent.\n\nThe MapStruct `OwnerMapper` maps the field automatically by name, so no mapper changes were needed.",
